<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Active vehicle for UMW_Storied (WeaponTraitDefs/Melee/Storied.xml), granted via
       WeaponTraitDef.abilityProps — see that trait file for the CompEquippableAbilityReloadable
       wiring. Self-cast, no target: the wielder plants the storied blade and calls out its history,
       and everyone not hostile to the CASTER in earshot/eyeshot steels themselves — the timed
       UMW_Rallied pain-dampening hediff via CompAbilityEffect_RallyAllies. Faction-symmetric with a
       stat payload per user directive (2026-07-24), replacing the original player-only +4 mood
       memory: a hediff is real for NPC casters where mood is inert, and symmetry makes a hostile
       wielder rallying its own raid correct rather than backwards. cooldownTicksRange 180000 (3
       days) is deliberately far rarer than Earthshake's 12h EMPPulse-parity cooldown — an heirloom
       moment, not a standing aura. aiCanUse true so a hostile AI wielder MAY rally its own side —
       but vanilla's ability-AI is only known to drive offensive abilities (every aiCanUse=true
       Odyssey weapon ability is offensive), so whether hostile AI ever actually casts a self-buff
       needs the in-game check alongside the §7 ability items; the flag is set so it can.

       PRESENTATION (all three parts land at the cast, none of them delay the hediff — decompile-verified
       2026-07-25, RimWorld 1.6):
         • The raised-weapon pose. PawnRenderUtility.DrawEquipmentAndApparelExtras draws the aimed pose
           for ANY Stance_Busy with a valid focusTarg, i.e. Stance_Warmup *or* Stance_Cooldown. Verb.
           TryCastNextBurstShot calls TryCastShot() — which for Verb_CastAbility is ability.Activate, and
           that is where our comp's Apply runs — and only THEN sets Stance_Cooldown(verbProps.
           AdjustedCooldownTicks(...)). So defaultCooldownTime lengthens the pose strictly AFTER the
           effect has landed, which is why the pose extension rides it rather than warmupTime (warmupTime
           gates Stance_Warmup.Expire -> WarmupComplete -> the cast, so raising it WOULD delay the rally).
           Cost, accepted: Stance_Cooldown is StanceBusy, so the wielder is rooted for those 2s (a
           player order cancels it via CancelBusyStanceHard) and a small cooldown circle draws under
           them — the beat of holding the weapon up is the point.
         • The speech bubble is a Mote_Speech via MoteMaker.MakeSpeechBubble in
           CompAbilityEffect_RallyAllies (Abilities/), not a def field: no XML hook reaches
           MoteBubble.SetupMoteBubble's symbol argument, so the symbol-less
           CompProperties_AbilityMoteOnTarget would give a blank bubble. See that file.
         • The shout is the inherited soundMale/soundFemale pair on the rally comp below, carrying our own
           one-shot copies of Core's throne-speech recording (SoundDefs/RallyingCryShout_*.xml — Core's
           own defs are sustainers and cannot be played as one-shots). It is the same vanilla source the
           bubble's symbol comes from, so audio and visual agree. Both land at the cast, gated with the
           bubble: see the comp for why base.Apply runs after the guards rather than before.
         • The sunbeam is the vanilla CompProperties_AbilityFleckOnTarget (preCastTicks 0 => fires from
           Apply, i.e. at the cast) carrying our UMW_RallyingCryLightshaft (FleckDefs/). It spawns on the
           caster because Command_Ability.ProcessInput passes `ability.pawn` as the target for a
           targetRequired=False ability.
         • The speech lines are Core's SpeechLines fleck, spawned from the comp on BOTH sides of the cry
           but shaped differently: over the caster it blinks on Core's own 45-tick ritual cadence in
           vanilla's centred south-facing orientation, for 3s rather than the whole pose (the line is
           called out at the start; the rest of the pose is holding the weapon up in silence), and over
           each responder it fires once, held to a full second via a per-instance solidTimeOverride and
           lifted clear above the head at a flipped angle. Neither needs a copy of Core's def. See
           CompAbilityEffect_RallyAllies. -->
    <!-- NOTE the pose duration below is read at runtime by the comp as a CEILING on the caster's blinking
         speech lines, so shortening the pose shortens the blink with it, but lengthening it past the
         comp's own 3s does not. -->
  <AbilityDef>
    <defName>UMW_RallyingCry</defName>
    <label>rallying cry</label>
    <!-- Deliberately silent about the waking side effects (user call, 2026-07-25): the gizmo text is for
         what the player is choosing to do, and the shout rousing sleepers is a consequence they can see
         happen. The mod-settings tooltips do spell it out, since the radius slider governs it. -->
    <description>Raise the weapon high and shout. Everyone friendly who sees it is reminded of the weight it bears, and for a time wounds barely slow them.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Commands/UMW_RallyingCry</iconPath>
    <aiCanUse>true</aiCanUse> <!-- faction-symmetric: an AI cast rallies its own side; see header -->
    <targetRequired>False</targetRequired>
    <cooldownTicksRange>180000</cooldownTicksRange> <!-- 3 days - an heirloom moment, deliberately rarer than EMPPulse's 12h -->
    <verbProperties>
      <verbClass>Verb_CastAbility</verbClass>
      <!-- Must match the comp's radius, exactly as Odyssey's EMPPulse matches range to explosionRadius
           and our own Earthshake does. VerbProperties.DrawRadiusRing (the ring Command_Ability.
           GizmoUpdateOnMouseover draws on gizmo hover) reads verb.EffectiveRange, NOT any comp field,
           and VerbProperties.range defaults to 1.42 — which covers the centre cell plus its 8 neighbours
           and was drawing a 3x3 preview for a radius-9.9 effect. -->
      <range>9.9</range>
      <!-- The comp requires line of sight to each ally, so LOS-filter the ring to match (as Anomaly's
           abilities do) — the preview then shows exactly who the cry can reach. -->
      <drawHighlightWithLineOfSight>true</drawHighlightWithLineOfSight>
      <drawAimPie>false</drawAimPie>
      <warmupTime>0.5</warmupTime> <!-- do NOT raise to lengthen the pose: warmupTime delays the effect -->
      <defaultCooldownTime>2</defaultCooldownTime> <!-- 2s of raised weapon AFTER the rally lands; see header -->
      <targetParams>
        <canTargetSelf>true</canTargetSelf>
      </targetParams>
    </verbProperties>
    <comps>
      <li Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.CompProperties_AbilityRallyAllies">
        <radius>9.9</radius> <!-- keep verbProperties.range above in step with this -->
        <hediffDef>UMW_Rallied</hediffDef>
        <!-- The shout itself. soundMale/soundFemale are inherited CompProperties_AbilityEffect fields, but
             the comp reads and plays them itself rather than letting CompAbilityEffect.Apply do it, so the
             caster's own VoicePitchFactor can ride along (that method's PlayOneShot has no pitch hook).
             Do NOT add a pitchRange to the SoundDefs to get variation instead: that re-rolls per play, so
             one pawn would sound like a different person every cry. A caster of Gender.None falls through
             to Props.sound, deliberately unset: silence is the right no-op, and a Talking-gated humanlike
             is male or female in practice. -->
        <soundMale>UMW_RallyingCryShout_Male</soundMale>
        <soundFemale>UMW_RallyingCryShout_Female</soundFemale>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_AbilityFleckOnTarget">
        <fleckDef>UMW_RallyingCryLightshaft</fleckDef>
      </li>
      <!-- It is a shout, so a wielder who cannot speak cannot make it. This is the same Core comp and
           the same capacity that Core's own abstract SpeechBase AbilityDef uses, and it disables the
           gizmo with the vanilla "X is incapable of talking" reason. CapableOf tests
           level > minForCapable, so any route to 0% talking gates it: a missing tongue, jaw damage,
           the Talking capacity's own zeroIfCannotBeAwake (downed/anaesthetised), a mute gene.
           NOTE this comp only overrides GizmoDisabled, which the AI path does not consult - the
           matching AI-side gate is CanCast in CompAbilityEffect_RallyAllies. -->
      <li Class="CompProperties_AbilityRequiresCapacity">
        <capacity>Talking</capacity>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </AbilityDef>

</Defs>
